Recovery demonstration — captured run
=====================================

Command : bash scripts/run-recovery-demo.sh   (passive / warm-spare mode, warning threshold K=3)
Result  : RECOVERY DEMO OK — the passive backup preserved 2 readings, was promoted, and fired the
          lane-departure warning on reading 3.
Logs    : target/recovery-demo-logs/ (full per-process logs); the key lines are reproduced below.

What this proves: the warm spare carried the lane-departure state across the failover. The primary
checkpointed 2 consecutive drifts to the backup before it was killed, and the promoted backup fired
the warning on the 3rd reading (count 2 -> 3). That is only possible if the backup restored the
checkpointed count; had the state been lost, reading 3 would have been count 1 and no warning.

-- primary (critical-service, before the kill) ---------------------------------------------------
2026-10-02 17:45:57 [INFO] critical-service: lane offset=1 m, assessment=DRIFTING_RIGHT
2026-10-02 17:45:57 [INFO] critical-service: sent checkpoint Checkpoint[serviceId=critical-service, seq=1, sentAt=1790977557432, consecutiveDriftCount=2, driftDirection=RIGHT, warningActive=false] -> localhost/127.0.0.1:5011
2026-10-02 17:45:58 [INFO] critical-service: sent Heartbeat[serviceId=critical-service, seq=2, sentAt=1790977558025] -> localhost/127.0.0.1:5002
(primary process killed here)

-- receiver (watchdog: detect then promote) ------------------------------------------------------
2026-10-02 17:45:55 [INFO] receiver: receiver-1 watching udp/5002; promoting backup at localhost/127.0.0.1:5011 on failover
2026-10-02 17:46:01 [WARNING] receiver: critical-service FAILED (missed 3)
2026-10-02 17:46:01 [INFO] receiver: critical-service FAILED -> promoting backup (failover epoch 1)

-- backup (critical-service: promote, then resume with the restored state) -----------------------
2026-10-02 17:46:01 [INFO] critical-service: promoted to PRIMARY at epoch 1
2026-10-02 17:46:02 [INFO] critical-service: lane offset=1 m, assessment=DRIFTING_RIGHT
2026-10-02 17:46:02 [WARNING] critical-service: lane-departure warning active after 3 consecutive drifts
2026-10-02 17:46:02 [INFO] critical-service: sent checkpoint Checkpoint[serviceId=critical-service, seq=0, sentAt=1790977562268, consecutiveDriftCount=3, driftDirection=RIGHT, warningActive=true] -> localhost/127.0.0.1:5011

